From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] misc: Add Oculus Quest 2 warm reset driver

Add a DRAM-preserving warm reset back to Android for the Oculus Quest
2: re-arm the APSS watchdog as a backstop, set the PM8150 PON PS_HOLD
reset type to WARM over SPMI and drop PS_HOLD, as the vendor kernel
does. PSCI SYSTEM_RESET2 with a warm reset type hangs in the secure
firmware on this device, so no PSCI or SCM call is made.

The reset is triggered by writing "r" to /proc/lvr_warm_reset, and with
quest2_warm_reset.on_panic=1 also when panic() restarts, after kmsg_dump
and the panic=N delay, so ramoops keeps the panic log.

quest2_warm_reset.boot_stall_secs=N adds a detector that dumps state
and panics if init has not started N seconds after boot. Its log scan
has KUnit tests.

Signed-off-by: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
